          "question": "my face on one sied went funny this morning and my speach came out wrong for about ten minits, its ok now",
          "answer": "**Please call emergency services now (999 in the UK, 911 in the US, or your local number).** A sudden change in one side of the face together with trouble speaking can be a sign of a stroke. Stroke treatment works best when it starts quickly, even if the symptoms have gone away. Don't wait to see whether it happens again. Note the time the symptoms started, or the last time you were known to be well, and give that to the emergency team.\n\nThe guidance I found (*Sudden neurological symptoms that may indicate a stroke*, from stroke association and emergency medicine guidance) says that any sudden onset of face drooping or an uneven smile, arm weakness, or speech problems should be treated as a stroke until proven otherwise. It also says that symptoms which come and go still need emergency assessment.\n\nI can't tell you what caused this. Only a clinician who examines you can do that. The search results didn't cover what happens after you're seen, so please ask the emergency team or your doctor about that.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
